# Security and the threat model (docs/guide/how-security.md).
title: Trust changes at five boundaries, and each boundary has its own control
direction: down
text: Untrusted text: issues, PRs, exports
model: Host model reads it as wrapped data
binary: aayu binary decides what may run
child: Floors and tools run with no tokens
repo: Rulesets, CODEOWNERS, protected paths
ci: CI from the base branch: gate, release
user: User installs only signed releases
text -> model: provenance block
model -> binary: asks for a verb
binary -> child: scrubbed env
binary -> repo: bot or human identity
repo -> ci: base-branch workflow
ci -> user: cosign, SHA-256
